  "restoration_note": "Teaching 28 enumerates the Twelve Judges sent forth from Greatness — the Lord's discriminating operation in twelve registers. The strict ordinal-judge formula ('The Nth judge is X, who...') and recurring formulas (†ⲍⲉⲡ ⲕⲁⲧⲁ ⲟⲩⲍⲉⲡ ⲛⲇⲓⲕⲁⲓⲟⲥⲩⲛⲏ, ⲡⲱⲣⲭ ⲁⲃⲁⲗ between victorious/destroyed) constrain most fills to high confidence. The titles of the judges are anchored in the lexicon (First Man, Living Spirit, Mother of Life, Great Builder, King of Honor, Third Ambassador, Jesus the Radiance, Virgin of Light, Mind of Light, Great Counsel). The damaged middle passage describing the Third Ambassador's discriminating action against the worlds of the Enemy (gaps 61–69, 78, 81) was largely too fragmentary; partial fills are offered with low/moderate confidence where antithetical structures (victorious/destroyed, light/darkness) constrain. Final epithets of the hidden Father at the consummation (99–103) follow the apophatic Manichaean idiom 'untouchable, established in the aeons of Greatness, set upon the great Throne of Honor.'",
